{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nRebar resolves configuration through multiple authorities during one operation, and some backends reread ambient state after receiving explicit config. Authentication is also composed inconsistently across LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, observability, and op-cert boundaries. This can change behavior mid-operation, discard an explicit choice, expose static credentials to unrelated children, or fall back through an unintended identity. RP-04 establishes one application-wide composition contract without making Rebar a credential store.\n\nThe approved research is on `relevant-liberal-xantus`; ADR 0098 is authoritative. Landed RP-01 (`08bcb1f9`–`f0275172`) is the LLM baseline RP-04 must extend.\n\n## Approved design\n- Resolve one immutable, serializable, non-secret `OperationSnapshot` at each operation boundary. Precedence is explicit operation input > environment > project config > user config > schema default.\n- Resolve repository root separately: explicit `repo_root` > `REBAR_ROOT` > Git top-level/current directory. Interpret winning relative paths against that root.\n- CLI composes once per invocation; MCP and Python once per operation; long-running processes also own startup deployment policy and live runtime bindings. An in-progress operation does not reread environment, files, cwd, or global config.\n- Compose subsystem-local `GitRuntime`, `LLMRuntime`, and selected `BridgeRuntime` bindings. SDKs/helpers own credential issuance, storage, refresh, expiry, invalidation, and native precedence; Rebar-owned factories retain transport/output policy. `LLMRuntime` enters only RP-01's existing `PydanticAIRunner` -> per-run `ProviderSession` -> one-Agent path. Preserve its budget, complete-or-omit retry history, cache/accounting, typed exhaustion, artifacts, tracing, usage, and failure translation. No arbitrary client/runner injection or second scheduler/owner/path.\n- Represent unavoidable static material with provider-specific, non-serializable Pydantic `SecretStr`/`SecretBytes` carriers, revealing it only in the sending adapter. Do not add a universal secret broker, central credential union, automatic keyring fallback, or application-owned cloud-secret retrieval.\n- Trusted same-capability children inherit ambient environment for Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA compatibility. Rebar never installs credentials through global `os.environ` mutation. An owning child receives its adapter overlay; unrelated sibling children remove exact secret names declared by other Rebar adapters. Deployment/container/process boundaries remain the primary isolation mechanism.\n- Static bindings rotate on restart/redeploy; SDK-native refresh remains SDK-owned.\n- Op-cert accepts exactly one of `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` (preferred) or `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`, validates before queue/worker/network/workspace creation, and copies the key into a process-owned 0700 directory/0600 file. Jobs receive context-local signer/principal/push-policy bindings. Remove runtime SSM/boto3/region coupling and per-job retrieval. Deployment may retain ADR 0049's SSM-at-rest source by injecting/mounting the resolved secret before process startup.\n- Fail closed when explicit provider/profile/project/auth composition fails; never retry anonymously or as another ambient principal. Preserve optional write-only Langfuse/OTLP observability's fail-open/no-op behavior.\n- Add a portable-local-and-CI AST ownership gate beside `check_config_reads.py`. It derives config/credential names from authoritative registries, rejects reads/reloads/defaults below approved seams, red-proves aliases/access shapes, permits only exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions, and reaches zero legacy exceptions at cutover.\n\n## Scope\nRP-04 only: central non-secret resolution/provenance, operation projections, runtime bindings, provider-native auth injection, static-secret handling, op-cert startup composition, all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers, ownership gates, generated operator documentation, migration, and canaries. RP-02/RP-03 and RP-05/RP-06 remain separate.\n\nExplicit corrections: CLI input outranks environment for `tracker.dir`; malformed config fails before effects; backends stop reloading; supplied Python config stays authoritative; defaults move to the schema; tracker layout reaches every owner; Jira Cloud write scope loses `DIG`. Other auth, redaction, retry, TLS, and output behavior changes require an explicit child decision and test.\n\n## Migration / rollback\nExpand in shadow mode, prove parity/deltas and non-leakage, cut consumers over behind compatibility facades, add gates/docs/canaries, then remove legacy paths. Before write cutover, disable shadow composition to roll back; afterward require the snapshot-aware compatibility floor. Stored ticket/bridge formats do not change, and parity diagnostics never persist credentials.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] CLI, MCP, Python, and direct reconciler paths produce equivalent non-secret behavior from the approved precedence/root contract; a captured operation is stable across environment/file/cwd mutation while the next operation observes the change.\n- [x] Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state.\n- [x] A portable-local-and-CI AST ownership gate derives names from authoritative registries and rejects direct/aliased `load_config`, ambient config/credential reads, backend reloads, and configurable adapter defaults below approved seams; exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions contain no post-cutover legacy entry.\n- [x] The LLM cutover injects provider-native auth/session capability only through the landed RP-01 `ProviderSession` builders; RP-01's one-run/one-Agent request budget, complete-or-omit retry history, cache/accounting, typed exhaustion, final artifacts, candidate tracing, usage, and failure behavior remain green in authoritative offline oracles and bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries.\n- [x] Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration; missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback.\n- [x] Secret canaries are absent from repr, equality/hash, serialization, snapshots, fingerprints, caches, provenance, exceptions, logs, output, argv, URL/query strings, subprocess siblings, and CLI/MCP schemas, verified at behavioral boundaries.\n- [x] Same-capability children preserve unknown ambient/native-chain variables, owning children receive only their overlay, unrelated siblings lose exact Rebar-declared secret names, and concurrent operations observe no global environment mutation.\n- [x] Op-cert enforces its exclusive startup sources, fails invalid composition before service work, uses a stable process-owned 0700/0600 copy and context-local signer, observes replacement only after restart, deletes only its copy, and has no application runtime SSM/boto3/region dependency.\n- [x] Generated config/security/operator docs cover precedence, lifecycles, restart/redeploy rotation, provider ownership, observability's exception, subprocess limitations, and deliberate behavior deltas; drift checks detect schema/docs divergence.\n- [x] Legacy ambient/per-job composition is removed only after focused suites and bounded live paths pass; rollback retains accurate non-secret diagnostics.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] AWS review-bot and reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries pass after cutover without credential leakage or unauthorized fallback. Epic comments record run/change IDs, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry counts, and redacted outcomes.\n  provenance: environment=hosted-production; principal=aws-review-bot-and-reconciler-service; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — AWS review-bot cast LLM-Review +1 on Gerrit changes 1905, 1902, 1901 this session; live reconciler check-access against Jira project REB returned every probe step PROBE_PASS; a hosted reconciler foreign pass was witnessed at 2026-08-19T16:34:03; bounded-live provider bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 ran review-plan with retry count 0, no unauthorized fallback and no credential leakage; redacted run and change ids and outcomes are recorded in the epic evidence comment.\n\n## Sequencing\nADR 0098 is merged. Create and link vertical implementation children with behavioral oracles and exact file impact before reviewing or claiming this epic."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787162126747289001,"uuid":"34d130f5-f6c1-460c-955e-b04b04830307"}